</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The experimental results yield several key observations: (1) GADL consistently ranks among the top performers across all datasets, demonstrating robust performance under varying structural inconsistencies. While baseline methods often exhibit sharp performance degradation under structural noise, GADL maintains high accuracy even with 5% edge perturbations. (2) Embedding-based GA methods (e.g., GAE, T-GAE, GAlign, GADL) generally outperform optimal-transport-based methods (e.g., Final). SLOTAlign, which combines both learning-based and optimization techniques, achieves competitive but suboptimal results compared to pure learning-based models.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Effectiveness: evaluation on real-world benchmarks</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the effectiveness of the proposed GADL method on two real-world noisy graph datasets with partial node alignment: Douban Online-Offline and ACM-DBLP. These benchmarks reflect realistic and challenging scenarios, involving distinct graphs with partially aligned nodes. We evaluate the performance of GADL and baseline methods using Hit@<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, which measures the proportion of ground-truth aligned nodes ranked among the top-<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> predictions. The results are reported in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Effectiveness: evaluation on real-world benchmarks ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Graph Alignment via Dual-Pass Spectral Encoding and Latent Space Communication" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
